WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.860
<i>The year is 2205 A.D.</i>

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:14.020
<i>To annihilate the History Retrograde 
Army, who scheme to alter history,</i>

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.670
<i>we, who were born from swords,</i>

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.400
<i>engage in mortal combat today as well!</i>

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.990
<i>You're not listening! 
Well, that's surprising.</i>

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:43.360
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.430
"This anime is about the 
stories of the Hanamaru days

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:04.220
of a certain group of Sword 
Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:18.850
What were you doing?

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:19.860
I'm sorry.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:42.510
<b>"Sa"</b>

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:54.260
Yo!

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.030
23 - Tachi 
<b>Tsurumaru Kuninaga</b>

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.490
Sorry I kept you waiting.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:57.880
Master!

00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:59.470
Tsurumaru has arrived!

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.690
Good morning, gentlemen.

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:04.920
Good morning.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:10.410
As you can see, the snow that has been 
falling since last night has piled up.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:13.740
There are also areas that have 
frozen over, so be careful.

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:14.870
Yes.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:18.200
We have new Sword Warriors to welcome.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.770
The uchigatana Doudanuki 
Masakuni joined us last night.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:24.880
And the tachi Tsurumaru
joined us this morning.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.190
Yo! Nice to meet you all!

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.350
22 - Uchigatana
 <b>Doudanuki Masakuni</b>

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:29.350
Where is the battlefield I'm meant for?

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:30.690
Tsuru-san!

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:32.550
I'm glad I get to see you like this!

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:34.350
Oh! Mitsubou!

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:37.580
Please do not let our master down.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:41.900
Everyone remembers what it was like 
to be new and unfamiliar here,

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.490
so please try to help them.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:44.820
Now then,

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:48.290
I will announce today's duty assignments, 
which were appointed by our master.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.240
Ta-da!

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.790
<b>Duties</b>

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:52.230
Horse duty: Ishikirimaru and Akita.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:52.410
<b>Horses: Ishikirimaru, Akita</b>

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:55.020
Field duty: Aizen and Nakigitsune.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.130
<b>Crops: Aizen, Nakigitsune</b>

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:57.710
<b>Sparring: Maeda, Gokotai</b>

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:57.420
Sparring: Maeda and Gokotai.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:00.170
Laundry duty: Kasen and Yamanbagiri.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:00.300
<b>Laundry: Kasen, Yamanbagiri</b>

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:02.970
Cleaning duty: Hachisuka and Midare.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.880
<b>Cleaning: Hachisuka, Midare</b>

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.890
<b>Cooking: Shokudaikiri, Nikkari</b>

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.880
Cooking duty: Shokudaikiri and Nikkari.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:09.120
Of course, I will attending to our master.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.640
<b>Attending to Master: 
Me!</b>

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:12.100
Do we get dispatched if we have no duties?!

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.610
Guess I'll go polish my gun, then.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.310
No duties, huh?

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:19.350
And, lastly, Kashuu.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:23.610
Take the two newcomers and 
show them around the citadel.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:24.980
What? Why me?

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:27.280
Master appointed you.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.610
Be grateful.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.380
That must mean I'm loved, then.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:34.370
Understood.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:36.610
Ahem!

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:42.330
Now then, so that you are ready whenever 
dispatch orders come, be sure to—

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:44.370
Hey, about showing these two around...

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.230
You're free today, too, right?

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:48.050
Hey, you guys!

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:48.340
Yes, yes, I figured you'd ask.

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.660
Jeez!

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.540
You should listen until the end.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:53.330
Whatever.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.760
I'm Kashuu Kiyomitsu.

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:59.900
I'm the oldest member of this citadel.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:01.070
Nice to meet you.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.370
Yes, same here.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.720
Y-Yes.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:07.190
Also, having had the same
 former master as I did,

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:09.150
this is Okita Souji's beloved sword...

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:11.440
Yamatonokami Yasusada. Nice to meet you.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:12.490
Nice to meet you!

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:13.400
Yeah.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:17.130
Well then, the citadel tour is starting!

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:20.740
On your left, you can see 
the open-air baths.

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:23.880
This citadel has open-air baths?

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.210
That's surprising!

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:28.750
This is great!

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:30.630
Now, on to the next place!

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:33.050
Scrub, scrub...

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.010
Elegance is freshly washed 
shirts drying in the wind.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:40.980
<i>I want to wash that.</i>

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:45.510
<i>I want to wash that cloth myself somehow...</i>

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:47.900
Yamanbagiri.

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:48.950
What?

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.530
That cloth?

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:51.700
Doesn't need it.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:55.030
This suits a copy like me.

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:57.690
What if I said I wanted to?

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:58.630
No.

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:00.300
I see.

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:04.840
<i>That cloth would be so much 
more elegant if it were white...</i>

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:08.580
<i>One day, I will wash it with my own hands...</i>

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.050
Okay, this is the laundry area.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.520
A gentle scent that is
 always with you

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.520
<b>Sterilizing/Antibacterial</b>

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:17.940
There's another one...

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:19.630
That's fabric softener.

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.910
Our master, who likes new things, bought it.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:30.110
Fabric softener?

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:38.510
It's so soft!

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:47.340
They even have cabbage here!

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.880
20 - Uchigatana
 <b>Nakigitsune</b>

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.880
21 - Tantou
 <b>Aizen Kunitoshi</b>

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.880
Oh! They look delicious!

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:51.840
I have heard that the snow 
cabbage, which can withstand

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.350
the cold of the snow, 
is exceptionally delicious.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:56.960
Nakigitsune, let's try a bite!

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:58.950
Okay.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:01.680
Hey, now! This food is for everyone!

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:02.850
Can we really eat it?

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:05.560
Nakigitsune says it's okay!

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:06.970
It's our secret.

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:08.480
I'll eat some, too.

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:09.930
Let's eat!

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:09.930
Let's eat!

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:11.650
Okay.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:13.750
And here are the fields.

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:16.150
You can really be self-sufficient here!

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:17.640
Huh?

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.100
Sniff, sniff.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:21.530
I smell something good.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.870
What is that smell?

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:34.200
Ah! It's this!

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.390
<b>Do Not Enter!</b>

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:37.380
It smells so good.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:42.250
That grass is called a "herb." Master's
 been really excited about growing it.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:44.840
Well, they'll get tired of
 it pretty quick, though.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:48.220
What's a "herb"? Is it like nanakusa?

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:50.310
Let's see.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:56.890
It clears your nose right up!

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.540
I can breathe so easily!

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:59.990
Looks like we can use this in battle.

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.690
Let's move on.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:05.910
You sure are cute, Mr. Horse.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:08.220
What is your name?

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:09.530
These are the stables.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:11.000
It's Ishikirimaru!

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.270
Tsurumaru-san.

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:13.700
I'm glad we could meet.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:17.260
I never would've thought that
you'd be tending to horses!

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:18.380
What a surprise!

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:22.130
Healing is my primary purpose.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.640
So, your essence hasn't 
changed, despite coming here?

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:27.200
Look.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:28.350
Tsurumaru-san and the horse...

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:30.480
Their eyes are sparkling.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:34.810
Kashuu-san,

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.010
does this horse have a name?

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:38.880
It does.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:39.950
Hanataro.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:41.110
Hanataro?!

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:42.900
Why is it called Hanataro?

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:45.330
For your information, it wasn't my idea,

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:47.000
so if it bothers you, tell Master.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.550
18 - Tantou
 <b>Akita Toushirou</b>

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.110
Hanataro.

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:56.210
This is the training room.

00:08:56.790 --> 00:08:58.510
So, this is where you spar?

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:00.230
I wouldn't be bored here, I bet.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:08.520
Training's great. That way, you can 
fight the strong guys in battles.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.440
Have you two had experience 
fighting in real battles yet?

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:12.430
Yes!

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:15.900
Now, attack me!

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:20.360
Jeez, let's keep going!

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:26.370
<b>Single-mindedness 
- "Sa"</b>

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:28.080
<b>"Sa"</b>

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:31.000
We're back.

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:33.240
Hey, you!

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:35.250
A g-girl...

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:36.440
Mr. Newcomer!

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:39.800
You're Doudanuki Masakuni-san, right?

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.970
19 - Tantou
 <b>Midare Toushirou</b>

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:42.970
I am Midare Toushirou, nice to meet you!

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:45.930
B-Boy?

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.620
Kashuu, I have something to ask you.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:51.530
What is it?

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:54.770
Can I throw these cardboard boxes away?

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:55.890
What? Why?

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:57.530
They take up too much space.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:09:59.930
Master wants to keep them, though.

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:01.730
Said they might use them some day.

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:04.190
Can't throw things away, huh?

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:07.100
Let's put them in the warehouse, at least.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:07.990
Doudanuki,

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:10.080
won't you help me out with that?

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.450
S-Sure.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:15.290
<i>At any rate...</i>

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:18.500
<i>A boy-girl?</i>

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:20.790
Hey, Kashuu,

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:23.260
what kind of person is our master?

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:25.450
Ah, I'd like to know that, too.

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:28.430
I haven't gotten to properly talk to Master.

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:30.940
Let's see.

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:35.320
They're a little sloppy, clumsy, unreliable,

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:38.650
and I don't often understand 
what they're thinking.

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:40.970
But...

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:45.390
They try their best and 
have their cute points, too.

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:49.280
Why don't we go see them?

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:50.090
Eh?

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:51.940
That's a good idea!

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:53.960
Master's room is around here, right?

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:56.130
Let's just go and surprise them!

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:57.840
No, that's not a good idea!

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:58.620
Wait!

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:11.030
All right, surprise time!

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:11.900
Hey, wait!

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:12.820
What?

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:17.770
Master! Why don't you put the books 
you've read back on the shelf?

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:20.710
Jeez, without me, Hasebe, 
you can't do a thing.

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:21.750
Hasebe is working right now.

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:23.490
Let's organize the things on your desk!

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:25.060
I see, Hasebe is a hard worker, isn't he?

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:26.190
You don't know where anything 
is this way, do you?

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:28.870
Ah, jeez! Master!

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:33.000
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:35.830
That was delicious.

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:38.470
Mitsubou, that was really good!

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:39.780
Thanks.

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:43.370
I always wanted to try doing 
something other than fighting.

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:49.690
It's surprising that we've all been 
gathered together to fight,

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:52.420
when we thought we'd 
never have to fight again.

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:54.640
It is a curious coincidence.

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:59.100
We were together for a bit during 
the same period, weren't we?

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:01.120
Oda...

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:03.020
...Nobunaga.

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:04.680
What?

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:06.480
Do you not want to remember?

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:09.970
That man—

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:09.970
That man—

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:13.060
What? Say what you have to say, first.

00:12:13.060 --> 00:12:15.470
No, please, after you.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:21.420
Just thinking about that 
man makes me angry.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:25.110
Upset with a young tea servant,
who made a mistake,

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:27.050
he decided to kill the boy himself...

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:29.220
When the tea servant was hiding in a cabinet,

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:30.980
Nobunaga cut through the whole thing.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:34.300
Who cares if it had been
 with his bare hands?

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:36.680
I didn't like what happened after that!

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:39.150
Giving me a name like Heshikiri and then

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:42.740
simply giving me away to some 
tactician who wasn't even a vassal!

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:43.690
What's with that?!

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:46.500
It's no laughing matter!

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:48.710
You hate your former master?

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:51.700
Mm, well, it's not really "hate"...

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.090
Are you serious?

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:53.830
Right?

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:57.580
I don't really have good memories, either.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:00.130
That man showed off his power,

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:04.010
always going on about how 
the world belonged to him.

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:10.390
I was handed over to him 
after the Battle of Okehazama.

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:15.760
He used to polish me and 
often kept me at his side.

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:18.730
It seemed he was very pleased with me.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:22.010
He carved his own name into my tang.

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:23.770
Oda Owari no Kami Nobunaga

00:13:22.790 --> 00:13:25.550
That is something that will never disappear.

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:29.280
I was merely something 
for him to brag about.

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:32.330
Despite being created as a sword,

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:35.120
I have hardly ever been to the battlefield.

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:39.070
But, you were dearly treasured. 
Isn't that a good enough?

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:40.910
Am I wrong?

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:44.080
How you want to be loved is 
up to each person, isn't it?

00:13:45.710 --> 00:13:47.280
What about you, Yagen?

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:49.880
Surely you have grudges, too.

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:52.590
You were always at his bosom, weren't you?

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:55.240
I guess. Many things happened.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:56.730
But...

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:57.930
But?

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:01.390
From my perspective, he was 
a straightforward person.

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:02.970
Hasebe.

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:04.860
You're attendant right now, yes?

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.140
Master's calling for you.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:09.310
Now then, I wonder what it is this time?

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:11.250
What?!

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:13.410
This time it's Honnouji?

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:15.630
Right, let's make the assignments.

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:18.330
Now then, what will the line-up be this time?

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:21.190
These six swords?

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:22.370
I...

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:29.060
We'll be leaving on a sortie soon!

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:30.820
We're going to that man's place!

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:34.700
I am the captain.

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:38.230
Everyone's here, right?

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:40.280
I am the captain.

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:41.540
We get it.

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:46.180
It's been decided that our next dispatch 
location will be Honnouji in 1582.

00:14:46.180 --> 00:14:47.540
Honnouji, huh?

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:49.590
The Honnouji Incident, then.

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:51.670
That's a nostalgic place.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.870
What does the History Retrograde Army

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.040
hope to accomplish by going there?

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:59.620
Attack Akechi Mitsuhide's army, 
who came to launch a surprise attack,

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.830
and keep Nobunaga alive.

00:15:02.140 --> 00:15:03.930
At least, that's what Master thinks.

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:07.000
Trying to make it so the Honnouji 
Incident never happened.

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:09.670
We don't know that, but...

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:12.800
We have to win, no matter what the cost.

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:17.510
We can't let history and that 
man's death be overturned.

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:20.560
You're saying it's better that he died?

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:24.570
That is where his life was 
meant to come to an end.

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:27.110
We cannot allow this mission to fail!

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:30.870
They really hate their 
former master, don't they?

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:33.940
It might not be that simple.

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:39.180
They seem pretty fired up. I guess 
we should try our best this time.

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:40.050
Kiyomitsu!

00:15:40.050 --> 00:15:42.040
Oh, I almost forgot.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:47.420
Master told me this earlier,
 but said to take our time.

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:48.960
What's that mean?

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:50.500
I told you earlier, didn't I?

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:54.130
I never understand what 
our master is thinking.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.640
Since we're going to the 
land of memories anyway,

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:59.100
I think Master just wants
us to feel nostalgic.

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:01.680
That's an unnecessary concern.

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:04.140
Let's just go destroy the 
enemy and come back.

00:16:04.340 --> 00:16:05.470
I agree.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:09.320
No matter what happens,

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:12.490
I expect you to follow my orders, 
as I'm both our master's attendant

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:14.240
and captain of the first division!

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:16.010
Off to battle!

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:24.910
Huh, so this is Honnouji?

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:29.490
When I think about that man
 in there, I feel depressed.

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:30.720
Come, now.

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:34.930
How about we go and see him now, then?

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:36.080
No, thank you.

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:39.260
It would be upsetting if he
 appeared in my dreams.

00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:43.630
It's kind of amazing that 
you hate him that much.

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:47.780
More importantly, Captain 
Hasebe, where is the enemy?

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:49.230
I'll leave scouting to you.

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:52.040
Nobunaga was attacked in his sleep.

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:53.240
If that's the case,

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:56.820
the History Retrograde Army will 
likely infiltrate just before that point.

00:16:57.510 --> 00:16:59.780
It should be soon,
if they're going to infiltrate

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:01.990
before the Akechi Army or Nobunaga notice.

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:06.650
So, that's where they are.

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:11.570
Everyone, the battle has begun!

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:22.590
This feeling...

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:24.390
It reminds me of the past!

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:26.090
My blood is boiling!

00:17:29.030 --> 00:17:30.810
So, you're my opponent?

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:35.450
I'll go all out, then!

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:40.360
Pretend to feint and then attack!

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:45.580
Piece of cake.

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:49.080
Souza-san, are you all right?

00:17:49.220 --> 00:17:51.550
I'm used to pain,

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:52.370
so this is nothing.

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:54.460
Souza, don't push yourself!

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:56.320
Retreat to the back!

00:17:58.050 --> 00:17:59.720
There's no use trying to hide.

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:02.200
I'll cut you down!

00:18:02.820 --> 00:18:04.630
Oh, so that's where you are!

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:07.930
You've got some nerve, trying 
to surprise the likes of me!

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:09.280
There!

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:10.730
You're wide open!

00:18:10.890 --> 00:18:13.210
I was a bird in a cage.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:18.430
But now, I have obtained human 
form and am fighting like this!

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:21.400
My new master is certainly something else.

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:22.700
Behold.

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:26.990
This is the carved seal of the 
devil who drives everyone mad!

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:35.280
Are you okay?

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:37.770
I am fine, this is nothing.

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:39.290
Good job, everyone.

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:40.890
Mission complete.

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:43.080
Hasebe.

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:47.160
Shall we go see it for ourselves, just once?

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:49.370
The Honnouji Incident?

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:54.030
Eh? You mean seeing where Nobunaga dies?!

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:55.540
Why not?

00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:58.610
Master said we should take our time.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:01.400
Are you sure you're okay 
with those injuries?

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:02.980
You should hurry back—

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:06.190
These mere scratches are not injuries.

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:21.050
They said over and over that
 they hated Nobunaga, and yet...

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:25.260
Words don't necessarily reflect how one feels.

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:27.040
Contradictory, isn't it?

00:19:27.550 --> 00:19:29.000
So that's it.

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:34.080
That's the reason Master 
said to take our time.

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:37.930
Yeah, you're probably right.

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:46.680
Good job today.

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:48.720
I'm sorry I caused you trouble.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.070
Not at all.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:55.620
Souza, how are your wounds doing?

00:19:56.070 --> 00:19:57.330
You really took a beating.

00:19:57.680 --> 00:20:00.180
I made sure to get properly repaired.

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:01.550
More importantly,

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:05.680
why are we having nabe in the
 garden when it's this cold outside?

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:09.010
Apparently today is the "New 
Sword Welcome Nabe Party."

00:20:10.530 --> 00:20:12.600
May I join you?

00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:20.780
We didn't end up seeing how he died.

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:23.870
He always was an extremely proud man.

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:27.820
That's exactly how I remembered him.

00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:32.930
Hey,

00:20:32.930 --> 00:20:36.050
there's this story that I heard once.

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:36.910
What is it?

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:39.510
Did you know they found no trace of Nobunaga

00:20:39.510 --> 00:20:42.970
in the remains after the Honnouji Incident?

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:44.150
I've heard.

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:46.130
They guessed that he'd committed suicide,

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:48.990
since there were no witnesses that night.

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:50.150
What of it?

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:56.020
Maybe Nobunaga escaped from Honnouji,

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:58.770
survived using all his power,

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:05.700
obtained the ability to live forever, 
and is still living somewhere, even now!

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:10.700
That's quite a story.

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:12.960
Sounds like something he'd do.

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:14.270
It does, indeed.

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:18.190
But, if that were true, I'd be jealous.

00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:19.350
Is that so?

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:32.020
If Nobunaga was alive,
and you could see him now,

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:34.350
what would you say to him?

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:41.020
There's nothing I'd want to say.

00:21:41.560 --> 00:21:44.870
What would I say to that man?

00:21:47.400 --> 00:21:49.290
For today, let's drink.

00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:50.230
I won't lose.

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:53.150
<i>I miss Okita-kun.</i>

00:21:53.690 --> 00:21:56.050
<i>It would be nice if he was still alive.</i>

00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:59.820
<i>What would I say to him if I could see him?</i>

00:22:02.600 --> 00:22:04.780
You were just thinking 
about <i>him</i>, weren't you?

00:22:05.420 --> 00:22:06.740
Maybe.

00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:08.730
You're an easy one to read.

00:22:08.930 --> 00:22:11.180
Your face gets this look every time.

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:15.480
A shooting star!

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:16.640
Huh?! A shooting star?!

00:22:16.850 --> 00:22:17.870
Where is it?!

00:22:18.360 --> 00:22:19.920
Where is it?!

00:22:18.490 --> 00:22:23.110
Ah, jeez, you were prattling on, 
and I couldn't make my wish!

00:23:55.030 --> 00:24:00.030
<b>More Hanamaru Next Week!</b>
